DTSTAMP:20261018T080922Z
UID:1006764
DESCRIPTION:<p>Following an acclaimed\, sold out run at London&rsquo\;s Na
 tional Theatre and a smash-hit West End transfer\, Rosamund Pike (<em>Gone
  Girl</em>\, <em>Saltburn</em>) brings her Olivier Award-winning &ldquo\;t
 our de force&rdquo\; (<em>Metro</em>) performance to Broadway in a &ldquo\
 ;searing legal drama&rdquo\; (<em>Guardian</em>) from the writer and direc
 tor of the global phenomenon <em>Prime Facie</em>. <br /><br />Jessica Par
 ks is a maverick London Crowd Court judge\; sharp\, compassionate\, and de
 termined to change a system she knows isn&rsquo\;t always just. But her ca
 reer exists inter alia (&ldquo\;among other things&rdquo\;) as she balance
 s motherhood\, friendship\, and the elusive notion of having it all. So\, 
 when an unthinkable event rocks her finely tuned life\, can she hold her f
 amily together &ndash\; or will everything fall apart?</p>
LOCATION:Music Box Theatre\, 239 West 45th Street\, New York NY 10036
END:VEVENT
